  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-08-16T17:09:47.692Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "First of all, maybe it's not search-specific, but web Input wide problem, Ctrl+C/Ctrl+V is not working here. For example if you already have video opened in browser and want to share it with your friends in world, you can not just copy-paste title of the video to the player, you have to type it.\n\nSecond, Unity UI with custom URL input field becomes very popular last times, but have some specific setup, works only for master, and also glitches some times. So, maybe it's better to implement custom URL here? Just copy-paste link to popup window and that's all. Unified URL interface for all players and no UI setup work for world developers. Easy. This is also can be more useful for VR users too because some times it's simpler to pull your headset up quckly copy-paste link from your feed on desktop and put headset back, than searching exact video by typing title. \n\nThird, search results is not very informative. Information about from which channel that video, how many views and likes/dislikes, when it was published, ... can be very useful when searching something specific. There is also no marks is video usual or it's live stream. Also maybe implement search for channels, show that channel videos and select videos from that channel?\n\nThen, what about other services, ex. Twitch?\n\nSo, current search feels very plain and dumb. 😞",
